	journal = {e615©TheAuthor(s)2023.PublishedbyOxfordUniversityPressonbehalf of Facultyof PublicHealth.Allrightsreserved.Forpermissions,pleasee-mail :journals.permissions@oup.com},
	year = {2023},
	abstract = {Providing mental health support and interventions through artificial intelligence can open up more significant space for young people to get good services. ChatGPT’s potential to provide first aid to young adults struggling with mental health issues is noteworthy. Despite its benefits and limitations, today’s technology can be a valuable addition to the mental health support available to young adults. DearEditor, Recent developments in artiﬁcial intelligence, particularly ChatGPT, have emerged as a popular topic of discussion. In recent correspondence, ChatGPT has been discussed in the context of serving as a link between artiﬁcial intelligence and education.1 In spite of the fact that the existence of ChatGPT has resulted in both positive and negative outcomes, ChatGPT is already being utilized in ﬁelds such asacademic,2,3 research4 andhealth.5 Wewouldliketohavea conversation about the various ways in which ChatGPT may beabletohelpraiseawarenessaboutissuesrelatingtomental health. Access to mental health services for young people is diffi- cult to obtain, despite the fact that the prevalence of mental health problems is growing. Because of this, they are turning to online resources to help them with their mental health concerns and to provide them with a sense of fulﬁllment.6 Additionally,ChatGPTisutilizedtoanswerquestionsregard- ing mental health. People also receive guidance and support fortheirissuesatthistime.Accordingtoanumberof studies, young people prefer using online resources because of the fact that they are anonymous, that they can ask questions, that they are usable and that they know who produced the information.7 ChatGPT, which is an artiﬁcial intelligence system, pro- vides satisfactory responses to questions regarding psycho- logicalwell-being.8 Severalpiecesof researchhaveshownthat ChatGPT is capable of displaying an empathic receptiveness while it is responding. When using an online mental health consultation service, selecting the appropriate response sen- tences can not only provide a sense of comfort and calm, butitcanalsopreventotherpotentiallydangerousactions.In addition, if someone asks about behaviors that can result in negative actions such as self-harm or suicide, ChatGPT will provideanexplanationof theimpactthosebehaviorshaveas well as a solution that does not involve harming oneself. In relationtotheprovisionof mentalhealthservices,ChatGPT also offers information on the various mental health services thatareaccessibleindifferentregionsof theworld. As an alternative to initial assistance for mental health problems, ChatGPT can provide a positive response. The challenge for mental health services using ChatGPT is to participate and give accurate and precise information as ulti- mately as possible through websites or online sources. Apart from that, OpenAI has tried to implement these safeguards in ChatGPT through their API Moderation API, which they hopewillensureaccurateresponsesanddatafromChatGPT. It can prevent the provision of hoaxes and biased informa- tion.9 In summary, ChatGPT possesses the potential to have a constructive impact on the growth of mental health aware- ness and to be of service to this endeavor. The information that is made available by ChatGPT can be applied to both the prevention of issues related to mental health and the provisionof ﬁrstaidinformationpriortoreceivingtreatment fromprofessionals. Downloaded from https://academic.oup.com/jpubhealth/article/45/3/e615/7185477 by guest on 11 October 2025 e616 JOURNALOFPUBLICHEALTH Funding WewanttoacknowledgeandthankthePusatLayananPembi- ayaanPendidikan(PUSLAPDIK),theMinistryof Education, Culture, Research, and Technology, Republic of Indonesia, for granting a scholarship to the ﬁrst author to complete this study(BPIIDNumber:202209091080). Conflict of interest Theauthorsstatedthatthereisnoconﬂictof interestregard- ingthesubjectmatterormaterialdiscussedandconﬁrmedthe dataavailableinthismanuscript’sarticle. References 1. Rusandi A, Saripah I, Khairun DYet al. No worries with ChatGPT: building bridges between artiﬁcial intelligence and education with critical thinking soft skills.J Public Health 2023;1–2, fdad049.https:// doi.org/10.1093/pubmed/fdad049. 2. DaiY,LiuA,LimCP.ReconceptualizingChatGPTandgenerativeAI as a student-driven innovation in higher education.Procedia Sci Direct 2023;1–7.Availableonlineat www.sciencedirect.com. 3. Adiguzel T, Kaya H, Cansu F. Revolutionizing education with AI: Exploring the transformative potential of ChatGPT. Contemp Educ Technol,2023, 15(3),ep429. 4. Dwivedi YK, Kshetri N, Hughes Let al. So what if ChatGPT wrote it? in multidisciplinary perspective on opportunities, challenges, and implications of generative conversational AO for research, practice, andpolicy. Int J Inform Manag 2023;71:102642. 5. Johnson SB, King AJ, Warner ELet al. Using ChatGPT to evaluate cancer myths and misconceptions: artiﬁcial intelligence and cancer information. JNCI Cancer Spectr 2023;7(2):pkad015. 6. Pretorius C, Chambers D, Cowan Bet al. Young people seeking help onlineformentalhealth:cross-sectionalsurveystudy. JMIR Ment Health 2019;6(8):e13524https://doi.org/10.2196/13524. 7. Horgan A, Sweeney J. Young students’ use of the internet for mental health information and support.J Psychiatr Ment Health Nurs 2010;17:117–23. 8. AyersJW,PoliakA,DredzeM et al. Comparingphysicianandartiﬁcial intelligence Chatbot responses to patient questions posted to a public socialmediaforum. JAMA Intern Med 2023;https://doi.org/10.1001/ jamainternmed.2023.1838. 9. Pratt N.ChatGPT Artiﬁcial Intelligence & Mental Health . Psychiatrictime s.com(13Apr2023,May22,2023,datelastaccesed),2023. SitiAminah1,2, NurHidayah1, M.Ramli1 1Departmentof GuidanceandCounseling,Facultyof Education,UniversitasNegeriMalang,Malang,JawaTimur 65145,Indonesia 2Departmentof EducationalPsychologyandGuidance, Facultyof EducationandPsychology,UniversitasNegeri Yogyakarta,Sleman,DaerahIstimewaYogyakarta,55281, Indonesia AddresscorrespondencetoSitiAminah, E-mail:sitiaminah@uny.ac.id https://doi.org/10.1093/pubmed/fdad065 AdvanceAccessPublicationMay29,2023 Downloaded from https://academic.oup.com/jpubhealth/article/45/3/e615/7185477 by guest on 11 October 2025}
